From bc7415c313ae864916d6ba67ba4b13d706f27b77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukin <mylukin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Apr 2026 10:55:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: 8 critical bugs from best-practice and UX review
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Thread bindings: bind/unbind now force-persist immediately instead
   of being throttled by the 15s touch interval. Prevents binding loss
   on restart. Also log warnings on bind intro message failures.

2. Image pre-analysis: clear analysisText when all images fail instead
   of leaking "(Image analysis failed.)" into the main model prompt.

3. Streaming cards: discard thinking-only cards on NO_REPLY/idle instead
   of preserving them as ghost cards stuck on "Thinking..." forever.

4. Delivery metadata: namespace channel adapter meta under channelMeta
   key to prevent Object.assign from overwriting chatId/channelId.

5. Media upload fallback: hide internal file paths (/tmp/openclaw/...)
   from users when media upload fails — show "[Media upload failed]"
   for local paths, keep URL for remote paths.

6. Context overflow: emit user-visible "Compacting context..." system
   event before sending /compact, eliminating 30-90s black screen.

7. Small context windows: skip "reduced" profile and go straight to
   "minimal" when context window < 30K tokens, avoiding negative
   available budget from the reserve=max(tokens*0.3, 30K) formula.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
